<header><p class="enc-kicker">State</p><h1 class="enc-title">Peloponnesian League</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Peloponnesian League was an alliance of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/greek-city-states">Greek city-states</a> in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/peloponnese">Peloponnese</a> led by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sparta">Sparta</a>, formed in the sixth century BCE. It fought <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/athens">Athens</a> and its allies in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/peloponnesian-war">Peloponnesian War</a>. The exhaustion of the Greek city-states after these conflicts created an opening that Philip II exploited in building the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/macedonian-empire">Macedonian Empire</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/peloponnesian-league.jpg" alt="Peloponnesian League" width="320" height="256" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Marsyas; derivative work by Aeonx · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Map_Peloponnesian_War_431_BC-en.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
